<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter II of Cyprus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1357–<a href="/years/1382">1382</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter II was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from 1369, after the murder of his father Peter I. At his coronation as king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in Famagusta in 1372, a quarrel over precedence between Genoese and Venetian merchants led to riots in which Genoese were killed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> retaliated with an invasion in 1373, and Peter had to cede Famagusta to Genoa and pay a heavy indemnity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="Peter II of Cyprus" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reinhard Saczewski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zypern-_Peter_II._-_M%C3%BCnzkabinett,_Berlin_-_5538438.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
